# The finish of a fold of two limbs (milestone2.md, "When something is not finite"): the final
# state when its leading limb is finite, with the flag true; otherwise the canonical NaN, (NaN,
# NaN), and the flag false. A finite leading limb of the final state means that every state before
# it was finite (the non-finite cone of the steps): the bridge of Milestone 1 applies step by step.
kernel:        fold_finish_2
input:         s = s0 s1
output:        r = r0 r1
output:        mask flag
value:         s
ensures:       finite_or_nan r flag=flag
min_precision: 1
source:        the finish of a fold: the state or the canonical NaN (milestone2.md)
license:       proof: MIT
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   proved
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeFoldFinish.v fold_finish_2_correct
cone_exempt:   the outputs are selects after an explicit test that s0 is finite (flag), which is what the kernel claims

a    = abs(s0)
flag = lt(a, const inf)
r0   = select(flag, s0, const nan)
r1   = select(flag, s1, const nan)
